{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774028992,"nonce":"TA62hOm8ZQ3qmhZJLJ4rElwgMJs=","title":"P3: CLAUDE.md updates — SDK-first tiers, architectural reflection convention","message":"Parent: f3dbb3e\n\nUpdate Mandible project CLAUDE.md with:\n\n## 1. Agent interaction tiers\nAdd a section documenting:\n- First-class (SDK): Console tab, full lifecycle + structured introspection. Default for all Claude interactions.\n- Second-class (PTY): Console tab, process-level control, terminal I/O. Used for codex, gemini, shell.\n- Third-class (External): Discovered via process scan or session hooks. Best-effort tracking.\n- \"Resume\" from issue detail always spawns first-class SDK regardless of previous tier.\n- Feature design targets SDK-first: new capabilities are SDK-only, PTY/external get what can be inferred.\n\n## 2. Architectural reflection convention\nAdd a convention: when making architectural changes to Mandible backend/behavior, agents MUST explicitly reflect on ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md (global conventions) since Mandible's behavior and the global conventions must be tightly connected. This is not just \"read CLAUDE.md\" (which is already standard) but \"explicitly reason about how this change interacts with the conventions.\"\n\n## 3. First-class interaction framing\nDocument that the primary way of interacting with Mandible is through SDK agents in the Console tab. PTY agents in Console are secondary. External shell agents are tertiary but supported. The inbox, work-unit model, and issue navigation are all designed SDK-first.","files":null}]}